{"id":"v5","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":5,"of":8,"title":"Doing it to yourself","titleHe":"בִּנְיַן הִתְפַּעֵל","goal":"Recognise hitpa'el — and the letter-swap that hides it.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"הִתְפַּעֵל is reflexive: the action comes back on whoever does it. Present begins מִתְ, past begins הִתְ."},{"type":"binyan","he":"הִתְפַּעֵל","en":"hitpa'el","note":"Reflexive — the action comes back on the one doing it.","verb":{"root":"ל־ב־ש","inf":"לְהִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"to get dressed"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבֶּשֶׁת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבְּשִׁים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"מִתְלַבְּשׁוֹת"}]},{"type":"text","body":"When the root starts with a hissing letter — ס, שׂ, שׁ, צ, ז — that letter swaps places with the ת, because the two are awkward to say in the other order."},{"type":"table","caption":"The swap","head":["expected","actual","meaning"],"rows":[["מִתְסַכֵּל","מִסְתַּכֵּל","looks at"],["מִתְשַׁמֵּשׁ","מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","uses"],["מִתְצַעֵר","מִצְטַעֵר","is sorry"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"With צ the ת also hardens to ט — מִצְטַעֵר, not מִצְתַּעֵר. It's the one form worth memorising outright, because מִצְטַעֵר is how you apologise."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"gets dressed","translit":"mitlabesh"},{"he":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","en":"wakes up","translit":"mit'orer"},{"he":"מִסְתַּכֵּל","en":"looks at","translit":"mistakel"},{"he":"מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","en":"uses","translit":"mishtamesh"},{"he":"מִצְטַעֵר","en":"is sorry","translit":"mitsta'er"},{"he":"מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","en":"misses, longs for","translit":"mitga'age'a"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["development","specifically, of all things","gets dressed","heart"],"correct":2,"prompt":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","translit":"mitlabesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["at all, in general","wakes up","three (m.)","on me, about me"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","translit":"mit'orer"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["and he said","looks at","already","but"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִסְתַּכֵּל","translit":"mistakel"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["what","don't (with the future)","ready, prepared","uses"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","translit":"mishtamesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["saying (introduces speech)","misses, longs for","roof","is sorry"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִצְטַעֵר","translit":"mitsta'er"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["morning","misses, longs for","decides","feels"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","translit":"mitga'age'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which binyan is this verb in?","options":["הִפְעִיל","פִּעֵל","פָּעַל","הִתְפַּעֵל"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["מִסְתַּכֵּל","looks at"],["מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","uses"],["מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","misses, longs for"],["מִצְטַעֵר","is sorry"],["מִתְעוֹרֵר","wakes up"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “uses”?","options":["שֶׁלָּהּ","שָׁעָה","מַעֲשֶׂה","מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","translit":"mit'orer","en":"wakes up"},{"type":"choice","q":"Why is it מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ and not מִתְשַׁמֵּשׁ?","options":["The ש and the ת swap places","It's an unrelated irregular verb","The root has four letters","It's a different binyan"],"correct":0,"why":"Roots beginning with a sibilant swap that letter with the ת of the prefix."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “looks at”?","options":["זְמַן","מִסְתַּכֵּל","אוּלַי","מַסְבִּיר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מִתְגַּעְגֵּעַ","מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","מִסְתַּכֵּל","מִתְעוֹרֵר"],"correct":3,"say":"מִתְעוֹרֵר","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “is sorry”?","options":["מִתְלַבֵּשׁ","אוֹתוֹ","דֶּלֶת","מִצְטַעֵר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “wakes up”?","options":["אוֹר","בְּבַקָּשָׁה","כֶּסֶף","מִתְעוֹרֵר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “is sorry” in Hebrew","answer":"מִצְטַעֵר","hint":"mitsta'er"}]}